From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:34:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] feat(api): list the tenant's audit records

GET /api/v1/audit-events returns the audit records of the caller's
tenant, newest first, and needs the read scope. It accepts limit (1 to
1000, default 100, like the list endpoints), pageToken and an optional
correlationId filter, and returns {items, count, nextPageToken}; the
token is only present when there is another page.

AuditLog.list_page pages by position (timestamp, then audit id), so
records written while a client pages do not repeat or skip records on
later pages. The opaque token carries that position and a digest of the
tenant and the filter; a token issued for another tenant or filter, or
one that cannot be parsed, is rejected with 400. The token is not a
credential: the query is always limited to the caller's tenant. A new
index on (tenant_id, correlation_id, timestamp) serves the filter.

The operation and the AuditEvent / AuditEventList schemas are in the
OpenAPI document. The Go gateway does not forward this path yet, so it
is only reachable on the control plane itself.
